      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1306384803,
      "text": "Glinus lotoides is a species of flowering plant in the family Molluginaceae known by the common names damascisa and lotus sweetjuice. It is native to Eurasia and Africa and it is known in many other places as an introduced species."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Glinus lotoides",
